Homebridge-Homematic-HAP
Copyright 2026 Matthias Einig and contributors

This product is a derivative of, and is heavily inspired by, the
following two works by thkl (https://github.com/thkl), without which
this project would not exist. We gratefully acknowledge thkl's years
of work on the HomeMatic ↔ HomeKit ecosystem. Both upstream works are
licensed under Apache License 2.0.

  * hap-homematic
    https://github.com/thkl/hap-homematic
    The standalone HomeKit accessory protocol bridge that runs as a
    Raspberrymatic / CCU3 addon. Its configuration model, channel-to-service
    dispatch design, multi-bridge instance pattern, ReGa script discovery,
    and overall architecture are the primary specification this project
    re-implements as a Homebridge dynamic platform plugin. The hap-homematic
    backup/import format is consumed verbatim so existing users can migrate.
    Copyright (c) thkl. Apache-2.0.

  * homebridge-homematic
    https://github.com/thkl/homebridge-homematic
    The original (now unmaintained) Homebridge plugin. The four-tier channel
    service dispatch (address -> device:channel -> channel -> device), the
    EventServer watchdog reconnection logic, and the BIN-RPC/XML-RPC + ReGa
    dual-transport split inform the modernized TypeScript implementation
    here. Individual ChannelServices/* files were studied as a behavioral
    reference; no source is copied verbatim.
    Copyright (c) thkl. Apache-2.0.

  * homebridge-homematic-asaw
    https://github.com/AlexanderSchmutz/homebridge-homematic-asaw
    A maintained fork of thkl/homebridge-homematic that contributed two
    robustness ideas adopted in src/util/sanitize.ts: defensive coercion
    of CCU datapoint values to finite, in-range numbers before pushing
    them to HomeKit characteristics, and the auto-detection of LEVEL
    datapoints arriving as 0..1 vs 0..100 (a CCU firmware quirk that
    otherwise produces 10000% blind positions). No code is copied
    verbatim; the patterns were re-implemented.
    Copyright (c) Alexander Schmutz. ISC License.

